Validation Rules
• Identifiers are unique within their type; duplicates are rejected.
• Mobile numbers must be 11 digits and begin with 010, 011, 012, or 015.
• Prices, quantities, and weights must be greater than zero.
• Ratings are between 0.0 and 5.0 inclusive.
• An order must contain at least one line item.
• Orders cannot be placed with a closed restaurant, or for an unavailable item,
or beyond available stock.
• Wallet balance may never go negative.
• Promotion codes are case-insensitive, must be unexpired, and at most one
applies per order.
• A promotion with a minimum-subtotal condition is rejected, with an
explanation, when the subtotal is below it.
• Only an available rider may be assigned an order.
• Only legal status transitions are permitted.
• A delivery address must belong to the customer placing the order.
• Menu input that is not a valid option re-prompts rather than terminating.
